# Studio secret rules. Paste at the TOP of a project's .gitignore, before the first commit.
#
# Order matters less than timing. A credential removed after it lands in history is a
# rewrite, not a delete, and every clone that already exists keeps the old copy.
#
# These rules stop at a nested repository boundary. A repo inside another repo inherits
# none of this and needs its own copy.

# Environment values. The repo carries names, in env.example, never values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# Platform and cloud credentials
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.p12
*.pfx
*-service-account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
credentials.json
gha-creds-*.json

# Anything named like a secret, whatever the extension
*secret*
*SECRET*
*_token
*.token
*credentials*
!*credentials*.md

# Local platform state
.vercel
.wrangler
.supabase
.sst
.aws-sam

# Build output and caches
node_modules/
.next/
dist/
build/
out/
.turbo/
coverage/

# Generated agent rosters. Build output from the studio, never edited, never committed.
.claude/agents/

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
